      "duration": 26.74,
      "score": 7.72,
      "text": "United States or Canada, which were 56% at the time. This is what the countries look like in terms of ranking by smartphone penetration rate. In 2013, Androids dominated the South Korean market. And this is what their Android looked like. The design for browsing internet is really not that different from that of an iPhone, which according to Answer in Progress supposedly changed Western website designs. So according to the argument made by Answer in Progress, South Korean internet should look similar to that of North America because we adopted similar technology around the same time. But a lot of Korean and Chinese websites look like this, similar to that of Japan. Some of the most visited websites in South Korea today still look like this. Why? It's culture.",
