      "end": 416.06,
      "duration": 33.28,
      "score": 7.44,
      "text": "This difference in how we process information actually makes a huge difference in how information is presented. In these two different cultures. The lens through which your brain sees the world shapes your reality. A group of researchers conducted a study that examined how people from different cultures present information to others. They found that there was a clear distinction between Eastern and Western culture in what is considered the optimal amount of information presented.",
